  "notes": "Official cause code is TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields even though narrative gives detailed root/contributing cause discussion (procedural lift/land rigor and inadequate PMT). AFWS actuated as a consequence of loss of last running MFP, not a backup during an inoperability window, so it is modeled as an involved/actuated system rather than BACKED_UP_BY. 'A' SUT reenergization of the bus post-trip is a recovery action noted in Safety Analysis, not a backup during the event window, so no BACKED_UP_BY edge asserted for it. No previous similar occurrence reported (explicitly stated none in past three years), so no SIMILAR_TO/stub LER emitted."
